      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of Dy(ClO4)3·6H2O (0.10 mmol) and H4L (0.10 mmol) in MeOH/CH2Cl2 (10 mL/5 mL) was treated with Et3N (0.40 mmol). The resulting red solution was stirred for 3 h and subsequently filtered. The precipitation was redissolved in DMF (~8 mL). Diethyl ether was allowed to diffuse slowly into the solution at room temperature. Red crystals of compound 1 suitable for X-ray diffraction were isolated after several weeks.",
